@page "/privacy"
@page "/privacy-policy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy | Comfidiario</PageTitle>
<SeoMetadata Title="Privacy Policy | Comfidiario"
             Description="How Comfidiario handles account, journal, cookie, and privacy-request information."
             CanonicalPath="/privacy"
             Robots="index, follow" />

<main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-document">
        <p class="legal-eyebrow">Legal and privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Effective for the current Comfidiario service: 31 March 2025. Last reviewed: 17 November 2026.</p>

        <section>
            <h2>Who we are</h2>
            <p>Comfidiario is operated by an individual based in Peru. Before public launch, the operator must add the full legal name, postal address, and monitored privacy email. The missing details do not authorize us to ignore privacy requests.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Law and data controller</h2>
            <p>This policy is prepared for Peru's Ley N.º 29733, Ley de Protección de Datos Personales, and Decreto Supremo N.º 016-2024-JUS. It applies to personal data that Comfidiario decides to collect and determine the purpose of. Other laws may apply where users or providers are located outside Peru.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account data:</strong> name, email address, password hash, creation date, consent records, and age-confirmation status.</li>
                <li><strong>Journal data:</strong> titles, entries, dates, and page information that signed-in users create.</li>
                <li><strong>Authentication data:</strong> security cookies and optional Google sign-in name and email.</li>
                <li><strong>Browser data:</strong> anonymous journal content stored in browser local storage.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> hosting and database diagnostics, connection details, security logs, and provider request information. We do not intentionally collect journal text or passwords in analytics or session replay systems.</li>
                <li><strong>Rights requests:</strong> copyright notices and support messages, including the contact details you provide.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Why we use it</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>To create and authenticate accounts.</li>
                <li>To save, display, edit, and delete journals.</li>
                <li>To protect accounts and investigate abuse or security incidents.</li>
                <li>To respond to support, copyright, data-protection, and account requests.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Journal titles and entries are not used for advertising or profiling. Data is not sold.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Legal bases and minimization</h2>
            <p>Processing is limited to providing the service, legitimate security and support operations, and your recorded consent where required. The international-transfer acknowledgement can be changed in Profile. Journal content should contain only what you choose to save.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Children and minors</h2>
            <p>The service is intended for adults. Registration requires confirmation that the user is at least 18 or has valid consent from a parent or legal guardian. We do not knowingly collect data from a child where applicable consent has not been obtained. If you believe a minor's data was supplied without valid authority, use <a href="/contact">Contact &amp; Support</a> or delete the account.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Security</h2>
            <p>Passwords are hashed with BCrypt. Signed-in journal titles and entry text are encrypted with ASP.NET Core Data Protection before database storage. This is application-level encryption, not end-to-end encryption: Comfidiario can decrypt it to provide the service. Authentication and session cookies are HTTP-only and HTTPS is required in production. Database and provider access must remain restricted.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Providers and international transfers</h2>
            <p>Comfidiario may use PostgreSQL, Azure App Service, Azure Blob Storage, Azure diagnostics, and optional Google sign-in. The deployed regions and providers must be confirmed by the operator. Providers may process or store data outside Peru. The application asks users to acknowledge this in Profile and discloses that processing in this policy.</p>
            <p>The application loads no Google Fonts or jsDelivr/GSAP script. Google sign-in is an optional provider and is available only when configured.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
            <p>Required authentication, session, external sign-in, and antiforgery cookies are described in the <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>. Anonymous journal content is stored only in browser local storage. The application does not intentionally run advertising, analytics, or session-replay trackers.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
            <p>Account and journal records remain until deleted or removed under a documented retention process. Signed-in users can permanently delete their account and associated journals from <a href="/account/delete">Delete account</a>. Provider backups, security logs, and notice records may remain for the period needed for backup restoration, incident evidence, legal defense, or request handling, subject to documented limits.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>Subject to identity and legal verification, you may request access, correction, deletion, information about processing, withdrawal of consent, or portability. You can:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Download account and journal data from <a href="/profile">Profile</a>.</li>
                <li>Edit or delete journals while signed in.</li>
                <li>Change the international-transfer acknowledgement in Profile.</li>
                <li>Delete the active account and associated journals from Account deletion.</li>
                <li>Submit a support or privacy request through <a href="/contact">Contact &amp; Support</a>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Requests should not include passwords or unnecessary journal content. The operator must establish a verified response workflow and preserve evidence of handling only as needed.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Database and regulatory registration</h2>
            <p>The operator must determine whether the personal database requires registration or notification with the Autoridad Nacional de Protección de Datos Personales and maintain a record of processing activities, security measures, provider contracts, retention periods, and transfer safeguards.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Copyright notices</h2>
            <p>Copyright and counter-notice information is handled separately through the <a href="/copyright">Copyright complaint form</a>. Details are retained only for review, communication, legal documentation, and abuse prevention.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Changes</h2>
            <p>Material changes will be dated and disclosed on this page. Public legal terms must be reviewed by Peruvian legal counsel before launch.</p>
        </section>

        <nav class="legal-page-links" aria-label="Other legal pages">
            <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
            <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>
            <a href="/copyright">Copyright</a>
            <a href="/contact">Contact &amp; Support</a>
        </nav>
    </article>
</main>
